# The independent read, and how each finding was taken

One read, by an AI reviewer (Opus) working read-only, 31 October 2026, of pass 1 of the four drafts (measured in [MEASURE-RUNS.txt](MEASURE-RUNS.txt)), against AGENTS.md, the live pages, the chapters' home sections and the glossary. Its report is below verbatim, then the judgement of each finding. Every finding was checked against the source it names before it was taken.

## The report

Two errors are new in this cut: the overview now defines "abides" so that it reads as begins-and-ends, and it now presents a consequence of constancy as its definition. Two more come from the live pages and should be fixed while cutting: T7 is said to have "no frozen test" when LA2 is one, and self-concern's ranking of the fishery collapse is called "with no premise". Several never-cut items are weakened or missing. All relative links and anchors resolve against `theories/becoming/`. No person's or AI's name appears in any draft.

Paths below are relative to `theories/becoming/`. "Kit" means the folder `/Users/ren/theories/_process/research/2026-10-05-generative-foundation-review/root-foundation/development/front-pages-for-a-person/`.

1. **[error]** Overview §1 (EN). "An occurrence *begins* where it continues nothing, *ends* where nothing continues it, *abides* where both hold, …". The cut removed the live sentence that "both" referred to, so it now reads as "both begins and ends". That is a flash, not abiding (`chapters/01-ROOT.md#four-marks`: "abides (住) where something precedes and something follows it"). The zh draft's "二者都不成立之处，它*住*" says the right thing but no longer matches the English. Fix: EN "*abides* where it both continues something and is continued"; zh, restore the live "在它既续某物又被续之处，它*住*".

2. **[error]** Overview §1 (EN and zh). "…and a class under which no continuation ends (a *constant* class) is exactly one lying inside its own core." / "一个没有续在其下终止的类（*有常*之类）恰是…". Constancy is defined as `E˘;R ⊆ R;E˘`. "No continuation ends" is its consequence (`«有常则续不尽»`), not its definition, and the converse is not shown (`chapters/01-ROOT.md#constancy-and-core`). The live page had this right. Fix: "A class is *constant* where whatever one member conditions, a member alike to it conditions something alike; under it no continuation ends, and a class is constant exactly where it lies inside its own core."

3. **[error][never-cut]** Overview §9 T7 row: "the lock proved in the model; actual metrics conjectured; no frozen test". Also §10: "…and any frozen test of T7", and both zh equivalents ("没有冻结检验", "对 T7 的任何冻结检验"). LA2 was frozen on 25 October and run. Every frozen verdict passed and the conjecture failed for that judge (`chapters/02-MAP.md#t7`, *Frozen test*; `chapters/08-METHOD.md#theses`, T7 evidence). This is inherited from the live page and drops a failure.
   - Row fix: "…; LA2, frozen, in one trained system: every frozen verdict passed, the bridge failed; no field test of reform events".
   - §10 fix: "a field test of T7's reform events".

4. **[error]** One page (EN and zh), fished stock: "the boats' own continuation already ranks a collapse that ends them below keeping the stock, with no premise" / "不需任何前提". The home law ranks so only for orders increasing in the standpoint's own continuation. The home calls that monotonicity "C's premise … placed more narrowly, not warranted" (`chapters/07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-what-self-concern-alone-ranks`). The overview correctly says "with no C". Inherited from the live page. Fix: "with no C" / "无需 C".

5. **[never-cut]** Overview §2 (EN and zh): "Keeping widening, read on a course's moments, is generation that loses nothing". The home holds only under two deciding premises, with generation taken under the one (`chapters/07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-keeping-widening-is-generation-losing-nothing`, `Steps.keepsWidening_iff_generation_losing_nothing`). The live page kept "under premises of deciding … under the one". Fix: "Read on a course's moments, under premises of deciding, keeping widening is generation under the one that loses nothing"; zh, restore "在判定的前提下 … 在'一'之下".

6. **[never-cut]** Condition on the root, in both pages and both languages.
   - One page: "held de se, the condition is the root's, nothing lying outside every center's line".
   - Overview §7: "…and on the root, where nothing lies outside every center's line (`«续无外»`)".
   - Overview §10 "The root and the ethics as one account".
   - What is missing: the class is "the one of that relation", and "Along a net with no cycle it holds only with one center, which nothing conditions" (`«续无外则同一中心»`, `chapters/07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-the-continuation-condition-on-the-root`). The live pages stated the acyclic limit twice. Without it, the partial unification reads stronger than its home.
   - Fix: add "under the one of that relation; along a net with no cycle it holds only with one center" (about 15 words) in each place.

7. **[never-cut]** Overview §9, test failures blurred.
   - T3 row: "for trained systems conjectured, partly supported". 08 records failures: CG1's C2, CG2's two predicted keeps, LA1's locked side in two of four settings, and the second forbidden case failing as first worded (`chapters/08-METHOD.md#theses`; `chapters/05-COLLECTIVES.md#t3`). Fix: append "; CG1's C2 and CG2's two predicted keeps failed".
   - T5 row: "tests on role-played judgments mixed". Fix: "VD1 failed every frozen rule; VD2: X1s and X2 passed, X1 and X3 failed".
   - zh likewise.

8. **[error]** Overview T1 row: "three tests passed, four failed". MQ1 and MQ2 each appear on both sides in 08, so there are five distinct tests, not seven (`chapters/02-MAP.md#t1`). This row sits under "Check at landing", but the wording itself is wrong. Fix: "passed in three settings and failed in four (MQ1 and MQ2 on both sides)".

9. **[error]** Overview T6 row ("seen half with Mathlib") and §3 ("Observed by level, with Mathlib, its variance and lag-one autocorrelation rise as the margin to a fold shrinks"). The home is one variable linearized about a rest (and the logistic model), with nonlinear runs not treated (`chapters/03-KNOWING.md#r-slowing-down-before-an-own-end`; 08 T6: "in the linearized and logistic models"). Fix: add "in a one-variable model linearized about a rest", and in the row, "in the linearized and logistic models".

10. **[error]** Dropped deciding hypotheses in the overview, against its own "nothing here is stronger than its home".
    - §5: "Readers reading readers carry no more than the first readers took in". This holds only where every later member acts alike whatever its own coupling (`chapters/05-COLLECTIVES.md#r-readers-reading-readers`). Fix: "Where later members read only earlier acts, readers reading readers carry…".
    - §7, living significance: "…it is equivalent to a seed…". The hypothesis "with some living claim and some standpoint" is dropped (`chapters/07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-metaethical-core-characterization`).
    - §7, alignment: "an act whose difference stays beyond the actor's coupling closure is selected alike…". Add "(under hypotheses the chapter states)" (`chapters/07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-the-gap-for-ones-own-act`).
    - §2: "Rest needs a least loss … (proved on the World model…)". The least-loss law is "any type" over any amounts (`chapters/02-MAP.md#r-least-loss-rest`).

11. **[error][link]** Overview §2: "a choice matters only at a *juncture* … ([junctures](chapters/02-MAP.md#r-every-loss-passes-a-juncture))". That law is `chapters/02-MAP.md#r-reaching-before-and-after-a-juncture` (`Branching.keeps_before_juncture`). The linked one passes a juncture only "up to double negation". Fix: link the right anchor.

12. **[error]** One page: "With significance a free parameter, no statement about the represented dynamics entails the condition, by construction". The home is narrower: a statement *reading only the dynamics and holding of some dynamics*, and only "where there is a standpoint and a formation" (`chapters/07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#r-what-the-dynamics-leave-open`). An unsatisfiable statement entails anything. Fix: "no satisfiable statement reading only the represented dynamics entails the condition, by construction". zh likewise.

13. **[never-cut]** One page (EN and zh): "None of the central results is new mathematics; …". The standing is dropped: it is an AI review of prior work, and the search was not exhaustive (`chapters/08-METHOD.md#known-results`). The live one page and the overview keep it. Fix: "An AI review of prior work, not exhaustive, finds none of the central results new mathematics; …" (+8 words).

14. **[clarity]** One page uses "the step of invariance" (not-done bullet 3) and "held de se" (bullet 2) without ever explaining either. Fixes:
    - In the *Scope* bullet: "Its content beyond what acting already presupposes, the *step of invariance*, counts losses that return to no one."
    - In bullet 2: "held de se (each center of itself)".

15. **[clarity][rule]** One page defines *generate* in 02's sense and later glosses 生生 as "its continuing generation" with no note. The glossary says that gloss means 生发, not this sense, and that 生生 is not 02's generation (`/Users/ren/theories/GLOSSARY.md`, rows "generation" and "生生"). Fix: "…its continuing generation (生发, not the map's generation) [AI reading]".

16. **[never-cut]** P3 (a correspondence not shown for actual selves) is named open in T8's home (`chapters/07-SIGNIFICANCE.md#theses`) but missing from the one page's still-to-argue list and from overview §10. Fix: add "with P3, a correspondence not shown" (+6 words).

17. **[never-cut]** One page: "some passed and some failed" is the only report of the theses' failures. It is weaker than "as they fell". If budget allows: "T1 passed in three settings and failed in four; T5's first test failed every frozen rule".

18. **[zh]**
    - zh one page uses "[AI 读法]" (ASCII brackets, three times). The live zh pages and the zh overview use "［AI 读法］". Use full-width.
    - zh one page renders T8 as "道是生生"; the zh overview T8 row has "方向是…的生生". Use one; "道" matches "the way".
    - zh heading "**C 移走了什么。**" means "what C removes". The English is "What C relocates". Fix: "**C 的前提移到了哪里。**".

19. **[link]** Overview counts copied without a check comment: "three with countermodels" (§6), "The five master laws are restated on it" (§10; the nearby refresh comment names only the derived and reach figures), "Eight premises" (§1). Add "<!-- Check at landing -->" or link RESULTS.md.

20. **[error]** Overview §2: "Arising without end needs renewal, and under balance and dissipation renewal from beyond…". The home says it needs natural-number amounts and fails with real amounts (`chapters/02-MAP.md#r-continuing-self-fed-from-beyond`). That is a modelling dependence AGENTS.md asks to be stated where a law depends on it. Add "(in whole numbers; with real amounts it fails)".

21. **[clarity]** Overview standings table: it has no "argued" or "conjectured", though §9 and the philosophical thesis use both. "A part's *margin* reads its draw with the rest's exchange held" is opaque on a first reading. Suggest "a part's margin is how far its draw can go before a dependent, the rest held fixed, loses support".

**Budget.** The English one page is at exactly 1,100 and the overview at 5,998 (`measure.py`). Additions above total about 35 words on the one page and about 90 on the overview. Suggested offsets:
- One page: shorten the "Change and return" bullet to its recurrence clause (about 15 words) and drop "(an illustration)" plus the clause after "such as the seabirds'" (about 15 words).
- Overview: §8's continuous-course example (24 words), §4's confined-rise and cancer sentence (25), §5's "Position does not protect…" (17), and the Fine and Wilf sentence in §3 (20).

The zh pages have room (954 and 5,336 budget-words) but must follow the English.

**Overall.** The drafts are faithful in structure and keep most never-cut items in both languages. Both ethical premises are named with their roles, neither is asserted, and nothing says the ethics derives from the condition. The frozen-rule caveat, the empty-axiom-report caveat and the AI provenance of the readings are all present, and no name appears. They are not yet safe to land. The cut introduced two definitional errors in overview §1 (findings 1 and 2). It dropped deciding hypotheses that the live pages kept: the premises of keeping widening, the acyclic one-center limit on the root reading, and a few scope clauses (findings 5, 6, 9, 10, 20). And it carries over from the live pages a wrong T7 standing and a "with no premise" claim the home does not support (findings 3 and 4). With findings 1–13 fixed, offset by the cuts above, the pages would meet their budgets and their homes.

## Judgement

All 21 findings were checked against their sources and taken. The table says what the source showed and what changed; "both" means the English draft and its Chinese edition.

